<title>HUNGARY: Sofia airport cargo trade down 1.2 pct Jan-May y/y.</title>
<headline>Sofia airport cargo trade down 1.2 pct Jan-May y/y.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo trade at Sofia International Airport in the January-to-May period decreased 1.2 percent in 1996 from 1995, according to data provided to Reuters by the airport.</p>
<p> CARGO TRADE (in tonnes)   JAN-MAY 96   JAN-MAY 95   PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL TRADE			  4,181	  4,230	   -1.2</p>
<p> --chartered flights		   81	    292	  -72.3</p>
<p> --scheduled flights		4,054	  3,938	   +2.9</p>
<p> --trucks				  46		0		-</p>
<p> TOTAL EXPORTS			1,857	  1,599	  +16.1</p>
<p> --chartered flights		   21	     94	  -77.7</p>
<p> --scheduled flights		1,836	  1,505	  +22.0</p>
<p> --trucks				   0		0		-</p>
<p> TOTAL IMPORTS			2,324	  2,631	  -11.7</p>
<p> --chartered flights		   60	    198	  -69.7</p>
<p> --scheduled flights		2,218	  2,433	   -8.8</p>
<p> --trucks				  46		0		-</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE			 -467	 -1,032		-</p>
<p> --chartered flights		  -39	   -104		-</p>
<p> --scheduled flights		 -382	   -928		-</p>
<p> --trucks				 -46		0		-</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE - Cargo includes freight and mail. In the trade balance, negative numbers indicate export deficits. Due to rounding, some data in this report could appear fractionally different in other reports by Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
</text>
